# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Every variable here is OPTIONAL — with none of them set the
# app runs exactly as it always has: fully client-side, all state in localStorage.

# --- Supabase (multi-device sync) ---------------------------------------------------------
# Without these two the app is local-only: no account, no network, no sync.
# With them, every cook signs up, joins a restaurant with a 6-character code, and the whole
# AppState syncs in real time. See "Two modes, same app" in CLAUDE.md.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_supabase_anon_key_here

# --- Google Gemini (AI recipe scanning) ---------------------------------------------------
# Enables "photograph a recipe → structured draft" in the Recipes screen. Without it that
# screen falls back to on-device OCR only (tesseract.js), which is what it did before.
#
# NOTE THE MISSING VITE_ PREFIX, and do not add one. Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into
# the JavaScript the browser downloads, which would make the key public on a deployed site.
# This one is read only by the server (api/scan-recipe.ts) and never reaches the browser.
#
# Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey, then set it in BOTH places:
#   - here in .env.local, for `npm run dev`
#   - in Vercel → Project Settings → Environment Variables, for the deployed site
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# --- Sentry (crash reporting) -------------------------------------------------------------
# Without this the error boundaries still work exactly the same — they just log to the console
# instead of reporting. Nothing else changes; lib/sentry.ts creates no client at all.
#
# Everything sent is scrubbed first (see src/lib/sentry.ts and its test): no console
# breadcrumbs, no request query strings, no email, and every Hebrew run — i.e. every
# user-entered value in this app — replaced before the event leaves the browser.
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=

# --- PostHog (anonymous usage statistics) --------------------------------------------------
# Without the key, src/lib/analytics.ts is completely dormant: no timer, no listener, no network.
# It is also silent in local mode, with the Settings toggle off, and under Do Not Track / GPC.
#
# This is NOT posthog-js: that SDK autocaptures the visible text of every clicked element, which
# in this app is ingredient / recipe / cook names. analytics.ts posts a closed set of events (app
# opened, screen name, an allowlisted action *type*) straight to the capture endpoint.
# The project API key is public by design (like the Supabase anon key).
#
# In the PostHog project settings also turn ON "Discard client IP data".
VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=
# Default is the EU cloud. A US project: https://us.i.posthog.com (already allowed by the CSP).
# VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=https://eu.i.posthog.com

# --- Scan endpoint hardening (server-side only) --------------------------------------------
# /api/scan-recipe costs money per call, so it now requires a Supabase access token and draws
# on a per-user / per-restaurant / global daily quota (supabase/migrations/0006_*.sql).
#
# The function reads VITE_SUPABASE_URL / VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY as a fallback — Vercel exposes
# every project env var to functions, so the pair already set for the browser build works here
# too and there is nothing duplicate to keep in step. Set these two only to point the quota
# check at a different project than the browser uses.
# SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Extra origins allowed to call /api/scan-recipe. Usually unnecessary: a request whose Origin
# host matches the Host it was sent to is always allowed, which already covers production,
# every preview deployment and localhost.
# SCAN_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://example.com,https://www.example.com

# ONLY for a deployment that genuinely has no Supabase at all. With Supabase configured this is
# never read. Without it AND without this set to 1, scanning returns 503 — deliberately, so
# that "forgot to set SUPABASE_URL in Vercel" cannot silently mean "the Gemini budget is open
# to the whole internet".
# SCAN_ALLOW_ANONYMOUS=1
